1.32.0: grain amount and grain size

Until now the amount of grain could only be moved by its side doors:
the camera, the film, --strength (which takes the whole look with it)
and a push. Two controls of its own:

--grainamount N, 0..4: a multiplier of what the camera, the film and
the development give. 0 none, 1 their own (the default), 2 double.

--grainsize N, 0.5..4: a multiplier of the camera's grain size. The
strength is held: the amount is rescaled so the deviation stays where
it was and only the clump size moves, which keeps the two controls
independent. Classic grain is never finer than a pixel of the render,
so sizes under 1 show on the coarse cameras, in the silver model and on
big pictures.

Measured on a flat gray field through 35mm-negative, grain alone
(render minus the grainless render), classic model: deviation 1.72/255
at rest, 3.36 at --grainamount 2, 1.65 at --grainsize 2; correlation
between neighboring pixels 0.03 at rest, 0.65 at --grainsize 2 and
unchanged by the amount. The silver model gives the same figures.

Both act in either grain model, are recipe keys, sliders on the page
(Development), query parameters of serve, superjuice options, super8ify
variables (GRAINAMOUNT, GRAINSIZE) and are carried into the darktable
style (no grain module at 0). They are not in a color LUT, like the
rest of the grain.

How: they are scene keys, and scene keys now carry the value at which
they change nothing (PjSceneKey.neutral): 0 for the 25 old ones, 1 for
these two. The options hold a multiplier less one, so a zeroed
PjRenderOptions is still "no change", and every front end that walks
the key table got them without being told. The page and the wasm
bridge, which dropped a key whose value was 0 as "unset", compare with
the neutral value instead: grainamount=0 is a setting.

Nothing else renders differently: with both at 1, or absent, output is
byte-identical to 1.31.3, and a recipe written before 1.32 has no grain
keys and reads as 1 and 1.

Housekeeping: five stray curve charts named -_CAMERA (written under a
broken derived name while 1.30.0 was being made) had been riding in
every tarball since and were committed with them. They are gone from
the tree and release.sh removes them from the repository.

New: pj_grain_rms() in the library (the deviation of unit grain at a
size), used by the renderer to hold the strength and by the darktable
export to do the same.

Tests: core (keys, neutral values, recipe text, and on a flat field in
both models: 2 doubles the deviation, size holds it and raises the
neighbor correlation, amount leaves the correlation alone, 1 and 1 is
the default to the byte); CLI (replay, pre-1.32 recipe, ranges, LUT
untouched, darktable style follows); serve; wasm; page.
